\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every fixed Kerr mass $M>0$ and nonzero $|a|<M$, is there a sufficiently small weighted-smooth neighborhood of its asymptotically flat vacuum initial datum in which data admitting a future C1 Lorentzian extension of the full maximal development form a meagre set?

